  "final_message": "`compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns 480. Running the code gave the same result.\n\n`service2.compute_fee` imports from only two modules, `pricing` and `discounts`:\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = 600\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off the gold rate of 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 480\n\nNothing imports `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
